   "subject": "Fst and Fis",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>Hi,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m working on a nice Dartseq dataset encompassing seven penguin taxa. I have completed most of my key analyses now, and have gone back to tick off some of the more basic statistics (global Fst and Fis).</div><div><br></div><div>I notice that many researchers generate AMOVA based Fst using Genodive... and I also note that you can import a Structure file into Genodive. My structure file that I generate with DartR does not work in Genodive, yet it worked in Structure (even though I did have to remove the loci names). I was wondering if anyone else has had this issue with this conversion from DartR to Genodive, or if there is an alternative software that is recommended to generate these statistics?</div><div><br></div><div>The script I&#39;m using to generate my Structure file is:</div><div><br></div><div>gl2structure(glpenguin, outfile=file.path(&quot;~/Documents/DartR/penguin.str&quot;))<br></div><div><br></div><div>DartR works great for most other things I&#39;ve needed it for - and it came at a perfect time for me to learn how to untangle and analyse SNPs (thank you!).</div><div><br></div><div>Tess</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
