     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-AU\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">da...@googlegroups.com</a> [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">da...@googlegroups.com</a>]\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tessco...@gmail.com</a><br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Friday, 30 November 2018 09:15<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> dartR &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">da...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [dartR] Fst and Fis<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br>\r\nHi,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I&#39;m working on a nice Dartseq dataset encompassing seven penguin taxa. I have completed most of my key analyses now, and have gone back to tick off some of the more basic statistics (global Fst and Fis).<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I notice that many researchers generate AMOVA based Fst using Genodive... and I also note that you can import a Structure file into Genodive. My structure file that I generate with DartR does not work in Genodive, yet it worked in Structure\r\n (even though I did have to remove the loci names). I was wondering if anyone else has had this issue with this conversion from DartR to Genodive, or if there is an alternative software that is recommended to generate these statistics?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The script I&#39;m using to generate my Structure file is:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">gl2structure(glpenguin, outfile=file.path(&quot;~/Documents/DartR/penguin.str&quot;))<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">DartR works great for most other things I&#39;ve needed it for - and it came at a perfect time for me to learn how to untangle and analyse SNPs (thank you!).<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Tess<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div>"
